// Title: Potential Persistence Via Mpnotify
// Sigma ID: 92772523-d9c1-4c93-9547-b0ca500baba3
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-21 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence
// Description: Detects when an attacker register a new SIP provider for persistence and defense evasion
// False positives:
//   - Might trigger if a legitimate new SIP provider is registered. But this is not a common occurrence in an environment and should be investigated either way
// References:
//   - https://persistence-info.github.io/Data/mpnotify.html
//   - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ggY3srD9dYs&ab_channel=GrzegorzTworek
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_mpnotify.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\mpnotify"
